WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:07.360
A man in San Francisco ran his car into a
telegraph pole.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.740
When the police questioned him, his description
of the event was as follows: "The pole was

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:19.279
approaching my car, when I attempted to swerve
out of the way and it struck me".

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:25.730
Was he lying, technically no, he was just
placing the blame upon the telegraph pole.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:32.670
That's just distorting the facts, real lying
however, requires, a whole new level of dedication

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.710
and cognitive thinking.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.900
From a scientific point of view, being a good
liar is tremendously difficult.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.620
So why do humans do it?

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:50.800
Let's find out.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.130
When children are younger they believe they
are constantly being watched by their parents,

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.829
who they see as authority figures.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:04.070
So for this reason, they're considerably more
inclined to always tell the truth.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:11.270
But as we get older we start experimenting
with not always telling the truth, this usually

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.880
happens around the age of 2 or 3.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.799
Studies show the average 4-year-old will tell
a lie once every 2 hours, but by the time

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:28.560
they reach 6-years-old, that increases to
a lie every 90 minutes.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.630
Lying is quite a difficult skill that were
not born with, we have to learn it.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:40.670
The more we lie the better we get at it and
the frequently we will lie in the future.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:46.869
The ability to lie isn't easy, it's something
that few species can do effectively.

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:52.759
Although scientists have found evidence of
lying elsewhere in the animal kingdom, for

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:53.759
example.

00:01:53.759 --> 00:02:00.039
Koko the Gorilla who is able to understand
sign language once ripped a steel sink out

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:07.859
the wall and when her handlers confronted
her about it, she signed "the cat did it"

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:11.320
and pointed at Koko's pet kitten.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.450
Animals lie to each other in nature to secure
an advantage over their peers, wether it be

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.160
food, territory or a potential mate.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:24.050
But no species is as proficient at lying as
us humans.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:28.310
But our brains don't find it an easy task
to accomplish.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:35.970
In order to lie our brain must hold two conflicting
pieces of information at once, those are the

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.770
truth and a lie.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:43.370
Our brain then has to suppress the true bit
of information, and then tell the lie without

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:48.840
displaying any symptoms that one is lying,
which isn't easy.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.120
Some people are much better at this than others.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.800
The best liars are pathological liars.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.360
Pathological liars are so good at lying because,
unlike the average person, they don't feel

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.380
a single bit of remorse for telling a lie
or even worrying about the consequences.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:13.060
They accomplish this by convincing themselves
that their lie is actually the truth.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:19.140
When a pathological liar tells a lie, they
believe in their mind that what they're saying

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.080
is the whole truth and nothing but.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.840
Which makes them so utterly convincing.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:32.090
At the other end of the spectrum of extreme
liars are compulsive liars.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:37.380
These are people who lie at the first given
opportunity, even when there's no obvious

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.500
gain or reason for doing so.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:45.360
Compulsive liars are much worse at lying that
pathological liars, even though they do it

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.430
on a regular basis.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:53.490
This kind of behaviour often stems from childhood
abuse, when they grew up in an environment

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:57.320
where lying was necessary for emotional wellbeing.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:01.690
But how did the act of lying originate?

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:07.070
Well like most human behaviour lying is a
product of evolution.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:12.250
Thousands of years ago the individual who
could tell the best lies and most effectively

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.760
manipulate their peers into doing their bidding,
would often get the biggest rewards, such

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:24.350
as, a bigger portion of the food from hunting
trip, or their pick of the women.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:29.540
And over thousands of years, through a combination
of practice and evolution, humans got much

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.050
better at lying.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:37.610
But even in todays age there are a lot of
advantages to being able to tell a successful

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.610
lie.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:45.160
For example, we often tell white lies to keep
a relationship running smoothly or keep our

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:50.880
superiors happy, for example, when your boss
asks you if you did that all important spread

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.600
sheet they asked for an hour ago, you could
tell the truth and say no, but to avoid a

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:02.860
good rollicking, you instead say yes, then
do it as fast as you physically can.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:08.630
But scientists say these small white lies
we tell every day often aren't as successful

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.880
as we may believe.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:18.200
In actuality research shows that most people
can tell when a person is lying 54% of the

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.200
time.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:26.980
But then there's the more serious lies, such
as denying a crime that you know you committed,

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.130
or telling your significant other there's
no one else when really there is.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:38.780
Whilst these may be morally wrong, they can
often result in reward for the person telling

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:44.680
the lie, so it's easy to see why lying is
often the first place that most people go

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:50.470
to in a sticky situation to get themselves
out of it.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:56.430
In short we lie because it can bring us many
benefits and give us an advantage over our

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.860
peers, often without consequence.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:06.210
However most people are in denial over the
amount they actually lie.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:12.580
Because of the inherently secretive nature
of lying, when asked most people won't admit

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:19.419
to lying often, but studies show that the
average adult actually lies ten or more times

00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:20.470
a week.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:27.980
But don't fear, there are ways you can tell
for certain wether someone is lying to you.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:34.310
Our body emits certain signals and symptoms
when we lie, which we can't control.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:38.940
Even the best liar in the world can't avoid
these telling signs of a lie.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.120
Such as.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:46.370
A change in breathing, when a person lies
they start to breath heavier, their shoulders

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.610
will rise and their voice gets shallow.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:56.010
Also a person will stand very still when they
lie, almost appearing frozen in place, this

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:02.410
is because the body is preparing for possible
confrontation, if their lie doesn't go quite

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.240
as planned.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:10.500
People will also change their head position
quickly when they lie, jerking it about unnaturally,

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.800
this will happen right before the person is
expected to respond to a question.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:21.930
The liar will also provide way too much information,
believing that if they talk a lot and be completely

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:26.450
open with you, you're more likely to believe
their story.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:32.270
So if someone is going on and on about the
same point, they're probably lying.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:37.180
liars will also touch or cover their mouth
whilst talking, it's a subconscious way of

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:42.090
their body closing off their mouth because
there is information that they don't want

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:43.120
to slip out.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.190
As well as their mouths liars may also cover
the most vulnerable parts of their bodies

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:53.600
whilst lying, such as their throat, chest,
head or abdomen.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:59.389
We often associate liars with not being able
to maintain eye contact, but research has

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:02.990
shown it's actually quite the opposite.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:10.759
Whilst telling a lie people will usually stare
directly into your eyes without blinking much,

00:08:10.759 --> 00:08:15.570
this is a subconscious attempt by the brain
at trying to intimidate and control the person

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.380
you are lying to.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:23.919
Oh and in case you were wondering, lie detectors
don't really work, at least not the way people

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:25.919
believe they do.

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:33.140
The word lie detector is a misnomer, because
they don't actually detect lies, lie detectors

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.360
detect increases in anxiety levels.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:41.979
And since some people are able to stay calm
whilst lying, lie detectors don't work on

00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:45.320
everyone, and are generally unreliable.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:49.980
This is mainly why they're not used by the
police to question criminals.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:55.250
Because well-seasoned criminals are particularly
good at staying calm under pressure, rendering

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.710
a lie detector completely inaccurate.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:04.510
Oh and truth serums don't work either, that's
purely a fictional idea portrayed in books

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:05.510
and films.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:13.959
But in real life there's no known substance
that can reliably make someone tell the truth.

